{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc 'cat /tmp/research_notes.md 2>/dev/null | head -100'", "aggregated_output": "# Research Notes: Hierarchical Transport Valuation Speedup\n\n## Goal\nReduce per-case median method time while maintaining NRMSE ≤ 0.01, Spearman ≥ 0.999, top-quarter overlap ≥ 0.98.\n\n## Baseline (canonical)\n- B = 0.5215s aggregate (from protocol.json)\n- My local single-case measurement: ~5.7s for N=3000, M=2000\n  - 3 candidate batches (1024, 1024, 952) × 2 reference batches (1024, 976) = 6 batch pairs\n  - Label cost: ~0.8-1.0s (190 pairs of ~100 samples each)\n  - Per pair: POT sinkhorn ~0.5-0.7s + GeomLoss potentials ~0.13s\n  - 6 × (0.6 + 0.13) ≈ 4.4s + label cost ≈ 5.4s total ≈ matches measurement\n\n## Key Optimization Hypotheses\n\n### H1: Unify dual Sinkhorn solves\nCanonical solves Sinkhorn twice per batch pair:\n- POT `sinkhorn()` for batch-level cost (for inter-batch transport Q)\n- GeomLoss `SamplesLoss(potentials=True)` for point-level potentials\nBoth solve the same Sinkhorn problem. Compute once, extract both coupling and potentials.\nExpected speedup: ~40-50% per batch pair.\n\n### H2: Accelerate label cost computation\n190 GeomLoss calls at ~5ms each = ~1s. Can we:\n- Use POT or simpler distance metric?\n- Use smaller subsets per class?\n- Use a proxy like average class centroid distance?\n\n### H3: Larger batches / fewer pairs\nCurrently 1024 batch size → 6 pairs. \nLarger batches → fewer pairs but each pair more expensive.\nNet effect depends on scalability.\n\n### H4: Log-domain Sinkhorn\nAlready confirmed slightly faster. Use as baseline improvement.\n\n### H5: Approximate the second-level transport\nInter-batch transport Q is small (3x2 matrix). Could we avoid OT here entirely?\nJust use uniform weighting?\n\n## Quality Gates\n- NRMSE ≤ 0.01 (1% error)\n- Spearman ≥ 0.999\n- Top-quarter overlap ≥ 0.98\nThese are fairly loose, so significant approximation should be possible.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/solution/method.py 2>/dev/null | head -50'", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"v8: GeomLoss potentials + POT label cost.\nSingle GeomLoss solve per batch pair gives both F and batchcost.\nLabel cost uses POT sinkhorn (~2x faster than GeomLoss).\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nfrom geomloss import SamplesLoss\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\nimport ot\n\n\ndef _label_cost(x, y, r, ry):\n    \"\"\"Compute label cost matrix using POT Sinkhorn (faster than GeomLoss).\"\"\"\n    xx = np.concatenate([x, r]).astype(np.float64)\n    yy = np.concatenate([y, ry + 10])\n    W = np.zeros((20, 20), dtype=np.float64)\n    reg = 0.1\n\n    class_samples = [xx[yy == k] for k in range(20)]\n    for k in range(20):\n        if len(class_samples[k]) == 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Initial batch lacks a label support\")\n\n    for i in range(20):\n        xi = class_samples[i]\n        ni = len(xi)\n        a = np.ones(ni) / ni\n        for j in range(i + 1, 20):\n            xj = class_samples[j]\n            nj = len(xj)\n            b = np.ones(nj) / nj\n            C = cdist(xi, xj, \"sqeuclidean\") / 2.0\n            C_max = C.max()\n            P = ot.sinkhorn(a, b, C / C_max, reg / C_max,\n                            numItermax=500, stopThr=1e-6)\n            W[i, j] = W[j, i] = np.sum(P * C)\n    return W.astype(np.float32)\n\n\ndef value(x, y, r, ry, seed=17, batch_size=1024):\n    torch.set_num_threads(2)\n    x = np.asarray(x, np.float32); r = np.asarray(r, np.float32)\n    y = np.asarray(y, np.int64); ry = np.asarray(ry, np.int64)\n    tx = [np.arange(i, min(i + batch_size, len(x))) for i in range(0, len(x), batch_size)]\n    tr = [np.arange(i, min(i + batch_size, len(r))) for i in range(0, len(r), batch_size)]\n\n    W = _label_cost(x[tx[0]], y[tx[0]], r[tr[0]], ry[tr[0]])\n\n    def cost(z1, z2):\n        d = torch.cdist(z1[:, :, :-1], z2[:, :, :-1]).square() / 2\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
